=== P3 Dashboard widget 0047 EnergySiteInfoWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin (repo pins 2.x; prompt floor 2.2.x) -- AVAILABLE
  (JDK 21 JetBrains JBR, Android SDK at %LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk, gradlew 8.14.5). assembleRelease
  produced a Release APK (see gate below), so the platform capability is present -- this gate is NOT a
  platform-capability block.

P3 core prerequisites reused: A1 theme/tokens (TeslaTokens/Spacing), shared component library
  (ui: GlassPanel/Icon/IconButton/PanelTitle/Caption/BodyText/CodeText; feedback: EmptyState/ErrorDisplay/
  Skeleton/FeedbackGlyphs; datadisplay: DataFreshness; charts: ChartFormat), S7/S8 Energy data layer
  (EnergyRepository / EnergyStore -> teslaEnergySites + teslaEnergySiteInfo), S10 i18n catalog, S11
  diagnostics Logger (view.opened), S8 BaseFeedViewModel/UiState/Resource cache-then-network contract.

Web source: web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/EnergySiteInfoWidget.tsx (THE spec). Native output:
  apps/android/app/src/main/java/com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/EnergySiteInfoWidget/
    EnergySiteInfoModel.kt   (pure parse + projection + registration; no Compose/Android/HTTP)
    EnergySiteInfoSource.kt  (data port + S7 EnergyRepository / S8 EnergyStore adapters)
    EnergySiteInfoWidgetViewModel.kt (combines teslaEnergySites -> teslaEnergySiteInfo onto UiState)
    EnergySiteInfoWidget.kt  (Compose: WidgetShell-equivalent header + WidgetDetailCard-equivalent rows)
Tests: src/test/.../energysiteinfo/{EnergySiteInfoProjectionTest(16), EnergySiteInfoWidgetViewModelTest(11)};
       src/androidTest/.../energysiteinfo/EnergySiteInfoWidgetUiTest(8).

Parity (web -> native):
  - States: loading skeleton; hard error + retry (ONLY on site-info error w/ no cache, web error={infoError});
    content (detail rows); empty (web WidgetDetailCard empty branch); stale/offline cached + freshness chip;
    catalog (sites) error degrades to cached empty + error chip (web shows no hard error for a sites error).
  - Rows (web entries.push order): Solar System (nameplate_power/1000 kW or em-dash), Powerwalls
    (battery_count>0 ? "{count} x {nameplate_energy/1000} kWh" : em-dash), Gateway Firmware (version, mono),
    Installation Timezone (installation_time_zone). Null values render em-dash (web value ?? '-').
  - Empty message: no linked site -> "No Tesla Energy site linked"; linked but data absent -> "No site info
    available" (web hasSites gate). isCompact (size.cols<=1) drops title+icon and caps rows at 4.
  - Registry: id "energy-site-info", category "energy", default 2x4, min 1x2, max 4x40 (EnergySiteInfoRegistration).
  - i18n: translation_widget_energySiteInfo_{title,solarSize,powerwall,firmware,timezone,noSite,noData}
    (all already present in the S10 catalog res/values*) + translation_common_{loading,refresh,retry} +
    translation_error_serverError_{title,message}. No hardcoded English in native code.
  - Diagnostics: view.opened with slug=EnergySiteInfoWidget (PII-safe, emitted exactly once).
  - Accessibility: refresh control + each label/value row carry contentDescription; title carries heading().

Documented deviations (Honesty Covenant #9 -- no silent drift):
 1. Gradle module is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts: projectDir=app); the prompt gate's ':app:' does not
    exist in this build. The gate below uses ':android:' (the same skew every sibling P3/A* log documents).
 2. Production files live in the mandated dir com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/EnergySiteInfoWidget/ but
    declare package io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.energysiteinfo -- a valid Kotlin package cannot
    contain a hyphen or a PascalCase segment, so detekt InvalidPackageDeclaration + MatchingDeclarationName
    are @file-suppressed with justification (mirrors the CostBreakdownWidget/ChargeStatusWidget siblings).
 3. Tests live in the standard src/test + src/androidTest source sets, scoped to this surface. The offline
    gate runs JVM unit tests; the Compose UI/a11y tests are instrumented (connectedAndroidTest, device-only)
    -- authored + structure-mirrored on the proven CostBreakdownWidgetUiTest pattern.
 4. Host wiring (grid placement) is outside allowed files; the widget binds the shared S7/S8 Energy feeds via
    an injected EnergySiteInfoSource (EnergyRepository / EnergyStore adapters, host-ready). Both feeds are raw
    SI JSON decoded in EnergySiteInfoModel (sites array -> first energy_site_id; site-info {data:...}).
 5. PRE-EXISTING, UNRELATED repo breakage -- NOT introduced by this change (git status shows ONLY the new
    energysiteinfo + EnergySiteInfoWidget dirs as untracked additions; no tracked file modified):
      (b) BatteryCellsWidgetTest.kt -- pre-existing unit-test failures (OTHER surface) -> repo-wide
          :android:testReleaseUnitTest is affected; this artifact's SCOPED run is green (27/27).
      (c) BatteryCellsWidgetUiTest.kt:7 ('assertExists') + DriveEfficiencyChartWidgetUiTest.kt:7
          ('assertDoesNotExist') -- unresolved refs in the shared androidTest source set (OTHER surfaces)
          -> :android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin is blocked. The offline gate does NOT compile/run
          androidTest, so this does not affect the gate. This artifact's UI test uses only resolved APIs.
    The old conflicting-overload defect (a) documented by earlier siblings is RESOLVED at this HEAD
    (:android:compileReleaseKotlin + :android:assembleRelease both succeed module-wide, no isolation needed).

